    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d9">

                <pb facs="0080" n="6" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg6"/>

                <head>Mr. Burnley to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-12-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 9, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> With reference to your note of the 8th
                    July, and to previous correspondence, and to Lord Lyons’s note of the 5th August
                    relative to the case of the Labuan, I have the honor to state that the agent for
                    the owners has recently written to me requesting information as to how his
                    client’s case stands at present.</p>
                <p>I perceive by the correspondence that the matter was to have been brought <pb
                        facs="0081" n="7" xml:id="pg7"/> before Congress, at its last session, with
                    a view to a speedy settlement of the claims of the parties, but that certain
                    testimony essential to a proper determination of the question of damages had not
                    been obtained from the consul at Matamoras, and that, therefore, to your great
                    regret, the case had been unavoidably delayed.</p>
                <p>As another session has now commenced, I venture to bring the subject forward
                    again in the hope that the settlement may not be far distant.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. HUME BURNLEY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
